  "slitCause": {
    "where": "tee + khaki (and sweater + khaki), right hip, x 624–627, y ≈ 790–816 — C's base-top side column (lab 1) beside C's exterior",
    "A": "the TOP took C's base-top side contour below its own hem as top paint (D-210 rule 2 takes every opaque pixel of the item's own base garment): the tee's picture leaves C's base there unchanged; in the outfit that line lay over the khaki — a double contour",
    "B": "the BOTTOMS lost their own side outline over that column: C's base-top contour explains it (no new paint), and D-210 keeps the closing and the outline band out of another category's base; with a shorter top nothing covered it — a 1 px background slit",
    "fix": "d223 (A): a rim of the item's own base garment that C explains and that lies beyond the item's outline (> EXPLAIN_PX + 1 from its new paint and base interior) is the base redrawn — not the item — unless leaving it out would enclose a hole (then it is seam material and stays: the shorts' side under the top). (B): the closing — a gap ≤ 6 px between the item's own core — may cross another category's base. No per-outfit mask, no general dilation, nothing painted",
    "left": "a 1 × 3 px corner at the tee's hem (F-011), a reported crossing"
  },
